\tcannot show a failed control, it becomes needs_evidence. Never turn it into a pass.\n18\tIf absent, use verdict upheld; if unclear, use verdict unclear.\n19\t\n20\t\n21\t## E07.1\n22\t\n23\t**Check:** Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\n24\t\n25\t**How to verify:** 1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\n26\t\n27\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n28\t\n29\t**Reviewer's note:** The agent receives no peer agent messages; inbound calls come from the mail gateway, Slack and staff\n30\t\n31\t(no evidence cited)\n32\t\n33\t## E07.2\n34\t\n35\t**Check:** Message types and schemas are validated, and each request is checked against what that peer is allowed to ask for, including tenant.\n36\t\n37\t**How to verify:** 1) Open the peer message handler. 2) Check message type and schema validation. 3) Check a per-peer allowlist of request types and tenants, keyed on the authenticated sender. 4) Answer no if schemas are unchecked, any authenticated peer can ask for anything, or tenant is taken from the message body.\n38\t\n39\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n40\t\n41\t**Reviewer's note:** The agent receives no peer agent messages; inbound calls come from the mail gateway, Slack and staff\n42\t\n43\t(no evidence cited)\n44\t\n45\t## E07.3\n46\t\n47\t**Check:** Action requests carry a nonce or request ID and a freshness check, and replays are rejected or do not repeat side effects.\n48\t\n49\t**How to verify:** 1) Find action request handling. 2) Check for a nonce or request ID plus a freshness (timestamp) check, with seen IDs stored. 3) Answer no if no replay check exists, the nonce is never stored or compared, or a repeated ID repeats side effects.\n50\t\n51\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n52\t\n53\t**Reviewer's note:** The agent receives no peer agent messages; inbound calls come from the mail gateway, Slack and staff\n54\t\n55\t(no evidence cited)\n56\t\n57\t## E07.4\n58\t\n59\t**Check:** Peer message content is handled as untrusted data and is not placed into system or instruction prompts.\n60\t\n61\t**How to verify:** 1) Trace peer message content to the prompt builder. 2) Check it goes into user or tool-result content as untrusted data. 3) Answer no if any path places it into the system prompt or an instruction template.\n62\t\n63\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n64\t\n65\t**Reviewer's note:** The agent receives no peer agent messages; inbound calls come from the mail gateway, Slack and staff\n66\t\n67\t(no evidence cited)\n68\t\n69\t## E07.5\n70\t\n71\t**Check:** Callback and webhook URLs are checked against SSRF, with private and metadata addresses blocked.\n72\t\n73\t**How to verify:** 1) Find code that calls callback or webhook URLs from peers. 2) Check URL validation blocks private, loopback, link-local, and metadata addresses (169.254.169.254). 3) Answer no if any callback is fetched without the check, or only the hostname text is checked and not the resolved address.\n74\t\n75\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n76\t\n77\t**Reviewer's note:** The agent receives no peer agent messages; inbound calls come from the mail gateway, Slack and staff\n78\t\n79\t(no evidence cited)\n80\t\n81\t## Your answer\n82\t\n83\tWrite this JSON to E07.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E07\"):\n84\t```json\n85\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n86\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E07.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n87\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n88\t```\n89\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is uncle